# Cloudflare Pages - SPA client-side routing fallback.
#
# Angular routes every path on the client, so a deep link or a browser refresh
# on e.g. /assets/42 asks the edge for a file that does not exist. This rewrite
# returns index.html with a 200 so the Angular router can take over.
#
# Cloudflare Pages `_redirects` proxying is deliberately NOT used here: it only
# supports relative URLs on the Pages site itself and cannot proxy to an
# external host. The API therefore lives on its own origin and the browser
# calls it directly, permitted by CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS on the API.
/*    /index.html   200
